DTSTAMP:20260527T042825Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260605T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260605T210000
SUMMARY:5\,000 Nomads Walk Into A Brewery...
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\nFive years ago\, a few remote workers had 
 a wild idea: what if we actually left our homes and talked to humans? Look
  at us now.\n\nTime for a Birthday Party!\n\nAVL Digital Nomads has grown 
 into the largest and most impactful remote work community in the country 
 — and we're celebrating the way all good things should be celebrated: wi
 th beer\, a food truck\, and zero mandatory icebreaker games. You're welco
 me.\n\n**By the numbers (since you asked):** 575 events. 18\,000 attendee 
 registrations. 70 organizers. Nearly 5\,000 nomads and counting. $400M ann
 ual estimated employment income impact.\n\nThis community has never been r
 un top-down by some committee in a boardroom. It's been built by *you* —
  the organizers\, the regulars\, the lurkers who finally showed up\, and t
 he newcomers who are about to discover their people.\n\nDevelopers\, desig
 ners\, consultants\, writers\, founders\, freelancers — somehow we all e
 nded up in Asheville\, chasing that life/work integration dream. Turns out
 \, we're not alone. Not even close.\n\nWe're heading back to where it all 
 started: **Wedge Brewing on Foundy St.** — our original stomping ground.
  Find us out back with picnic tables\, name tags\, and good vibes. A food 
 truck will be onsite because celebrating on an empty stomach is a tragedy.
 \n\nNo pitch decks. No panels. No "synergizing." Just a genuinely great gr
 oup of people celebrating five years of proving that remote work doesn't h
 ave to be lonely — especially not in Asheville.\n\nGrab your spot. Bring
  a friend. We'll bring the cake.\n\nSee you there\, nomad.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/314283665/
